cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  foliar-fem: continuous geometry and anisotropic diffusion over the leaf blade
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Malla Campoverde
    given-names: Manuel Josue
    affiliation: Universidad Tecnica de Machala, Machala, Ecuador
  - family-names: Tusa
    given-names: Eduardo
    affiliation: Universidad Tecnica de Machala, Machala, Ecuador
repository-code: "https://github.com/jossuema/foliar-fem"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that goes from 2D segmentation masks of a banana leaf with black
  sigatoka to agronomic parameters, by way of constrained Delaunay triangulation
  and P1 finite element operators. On top of that infrastructure it solves an
  anisotropic reaction-diffusion equation modelling lesion expansion, with a
  latency compartment that anchors the time axis to the published biology of
  Pseudocercospora fijiensis.
keywords:
  - plant pathology
  - black sigatoka
  - Pseudocercospora fijiensis
  - finite elements
  - geodesic distances
  - reaction-diffusion
  - precision agriculture
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
